				<div>
					<h3 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.35rem; color: var(--accent-red); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
						📏 The Golden Rule of Variety vs. Headcount
					</h3>
					<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin-bottom: 1rem;">
						Couples often make the mistake of ordering 10 to 12 different dessert types in tiny 20-piece batches. This causes two major issues: popular items run out within 5 minutes (leaving disappointed guests), and lengthy decision paralysis creates bottlenecks around the table.
					</p>
					
					<div style="background: var(--bg-paper); border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.85rem; font-size: 0.88rem;">
						<ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.6;">
							<li><strong>50–75 Guests:</strong> 3 to 4 varieties (e.g. macarons, mini cupcakes, fruit tarts)</li>
							<li><strong>75–125 Guests:</strong> 4 to 5 varieties (adds shooters or truffles)</li>
							<li><strong>125–200 Guests:</strong> 5 to 7 varieties (adds cannoli, cake pops, donuts)</li>
							<li><strong>200+ Guests:</strong> 6 to 8 varieties maximum (deep quantity buffers per item)</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div>
					<h3 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.35rem; color: var(--accent-blue); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
						🍪 The Pittsburgh & Italian Cookie Table Tradition
					</h3>
					<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin-bottom: 1rem;">
						In Western Pennsylvania, Eastern Ohio, and Italian-American communities, the Wedding Cookie Table is an emotional centerpiece. Grandmothers, aunts, and bridal party members spend weeks baking heritage recipes: pizzelles, ladylocks, buckeyes, ricotta cookies, and Russian tea cakes.
					</p>
					
					<div style="background: var(--bg-paper); border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.85rem; font-size: 0.88rem;">
						<p style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;"><strong>Cookie Table Golden Rules:</strong></p>
						<ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.5;">
							<li>Plan for <strong>6 to 8 cookies per guest</strong> for the evening dessert.</li>
							<li>Provide cute kraft boxes or bakery bags so guests take home <strong>4 to 6 cookies</strong> as wedding favors.</li>
							<li>Keep the table closed until after dinner to prevent early clearing!</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>

