							<tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0;">
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px; font-weight: 700;">Real Buttercream & Cream Tarts</td>
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px; color: var(--accent-red); font-weight: 600;">75°F (24°C)</td>
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px;">Sliding, melting, souring dairy</td>
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px;">Keep chilled until 30 min before reception dinner ends.</td>
							</tr>
							<tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0; background: #f8fafc;">
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px; font-weight: 700;">Chocolate Truffles & Ganache</td>
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px; color: var(--accent-red); font-weight: 600;">72°F (22°C)</td>
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px;">Melts on fingers, bloom streaks</td>
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px;">Place in fluted candy cups in shaded, air-conditioned zones.</td>
							</tr>
							<tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0;">
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px; font-weight: 700;">French Macarons</td>
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px; color: var(--accent-blue); font-weight: 600;">78°F (26°C)</td>
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px;">High humidity turns shells gummy</td>
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px;">Keep in airtight container until immediate table staging.</td>
							</tr>
							<tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0; background: #f8fafc;">
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px; font-weight: 700;">Mini Cannoli</td>
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px; color: var(--accent-red); font-weight: 600;">70°F (21°C)</td>
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px;">Shell becomes soggy within 2 hours</td>
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px;">Fill shells on-site or request chocolate-lined shells.</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px; font-weight: 700;">Cookies, Brownies & Bulk Candy</td>
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px; color: #16a34a; font-weight: 600;">85°F+ (29°C+)</td>
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px;">Gummies can stick together in sun</td>
								<td style="padding: 8px 10px;">Ideal for hot outdoor summer garden and marquee weddings!</td>
							</tr>
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- FAQ Accordion / Grid -->
			<div>
				<h3 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.5rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin-bottom: 1rem; text-align: center;">
					❓ Frequently Asked Questions About Wedding Dessert Bars
				</h3>
				<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem;">
					
					<div style="background: #fff; border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1rem;">
						<strong class="font-heading" style="color: var(--fg-pencil); display: block; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0.3rem;">
							How early should you open the dessert table?
						</strong>
						<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0; line-height: 1.45;">
							Open the dessert table immediately following the official cake-cutting ceremony or after dinner coffee service begins. Opening too early encourages guests to graze before dinner, ruining appetite for main catering.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div style="background: #fff; border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1rem;">
						<strong class="font-heading" style="color: var(--fg-pencil); display: block; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0.3rem;">
							What size favor bag is best for a candy bar?
						</strong>
						<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0; line-height: 1.45;">
							A 4" x 6" glassine or kraft bag comfortably holds 4 to 5 ounces (0.25 to 0.3 lbs) of candy. Avoid massive 6x9 bags or large takeout pails unless you have purchased 50% extra candy, as guests naturally fill bags to the brim.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div style="background: #fff; border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1rem;">
						<strong class="font-heading" style="color: var(--fg-pencil); display: block; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0.3rem;">
							How do I prevent cross-contamination for gluten or nut allergies?
						</strong>
						<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0; line-height: 1.45;">
							Dedicate separate pedestal platters for Gluten-Free (e.g. macarons) and Nut-Free items. Use individual serving tongs for each platter, and display clear dietary tent cards directly next to each dish.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div style="background: #fff; border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1rem;">
						<strong class="font-heading" style="color: var(--fg-pencil); display: block; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 0.3rem;">
							Can we freeze leftovers from the dessert table?
						</strong>
						<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0; line-height: 1.45;">
							Yes! Handcrafted cookies, brownies, macarons, and cake pops freeze beautifully for up to 3 months in airtight containers with parchment paper between layers. Avoid freezing custards, cream puffs, or fresh fruit tarts.
						</p>
					</div>

				</div>
			</div>

		</section>

		<!-- Related Tools Component -->
		<RelatedTools currentPath="/wedding-dessert-table-calculator" category="food-beverage" />

	</main>

	<!-- Hidden Print Containers for Vector PDF / Window.print -->
	<div id="print-root" class="print-only">
		<!-- Page 1: Framed Love is Sweet Bar Sign -->
		<div id="print-sign-container" class="print-page" style="page-break-after: always; break-after: page; page-break-inside: avoid; break-inside: avoid; padding: 10mm 15mm; text-align: center; box-sizing: border-box;">
			<div id="print-sign-box" style="border: 4px double #000; padding: 18mm 14mm; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 190mm; max-height: 230mm; box-sizing: border-box; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; align-items: center;">
				<span style="font-size: 26pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; line-height: 1;">✨ 🧁 ✨</span>
				<h1 id="print-sign-title" style="font-size: 32pt; font-family: 'Georgia', serif; margin: 0 0 12pt 0; text-transform: none; color: #000; line-height: 1.15;">Love is Sweet</h1>
				<p id="print-sign-sub" style="font-size: 16pt; font-style: italic; margin: 0 0 18pt 0; color: #333;">Please take a treat!</p>
				<div style="width: 60mm; height: 1.5pt; background: #000; margin: 0 auto 16pt;"></div>
				<h2 id="print-sign-names" style="font-size: 16pt; letter-spacing: 2pt; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 0 0 6pt 0; color: #000;">Emma & Liam</h2>
				<p id="print-sign-date" style="font-size: 12pt; color: #555; margin: 0;">October 18, 2026</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<!-- Pages 2+: Foldable Dietary & Flavor Tent Cards (4 per page in 2x2 grid) -->
		<div id="print-tent-sheets-container">
			<!-- Dynamically injected by renderDietaryCardsPreview() -->
